# Static libraries are BUILD OUTPUT and must not be committed: this repo used to carry 22 MB of
# Limbo .a across three duplicate locations. Limbo is a submodule now (third_party/Limbo), built
# by vck5000/tools/bootstrap_third_party.sh.
*.a
*.out
python/AIEmath
python/results
results
*:Zone.Identifier
*.cfg
.vscode
misc
*.swp
*.db
.Xil/
Map_Report.csv
build/
.ipcache/
*.log
*.jou
*core.*
results/
temp/

# editor / tooling junk
__pycache__/
/tat
/vck5000/bin/
/vck5000/.claude/
# stray host build output (the real output goes to build/)
/vck5000/host/src/objs/

# Scratch output of `make test-regress`. The committed part of that test is
# test/regress/{configs,baselines}/; this is just where the run under test lands.
/vck5000/test/regress/work/

# Limbo (third_party/Limbo) is a SUBMODULE and is built OUT OF TREE, so the checkout itself
# stays pristine and can never show a spurious diff. These two are that build's output; both are
# produced by vck5000/tools/bootstrap_third_party.sh and neither belongs in git.
/third_party/limbo_build/
/third_party/limbo_install/

# AIE compiler workdirs and simulator/golden output
/vck5000/aie/Work/
/vck5000/aie/x86simulator_output/
/vck5000/aie/golden_data/

# Numbered workflow dirs (N_CAPSNAME: 0_OVERNIGHT_WORK, 1_REVIEW, 2_ARTIFACTS, ...):
# local async handoff / scratch between Mark & Claude, never tracked.
#
# The catch-all must match at ANY depth (no leading slash) -- these dirs live under vck5000/.
# The leading slash added by the MARK_TO_REVIEW -> REVIEW rename stopped it matching
# vck5000/1_REVIEW and vck5000/2_ARTIFACTS, which then sat untracked-but-NOT-ignored,
# including ~80 MB of GIFs that a `git add -A` would have swept in.
#
# 2026-08-07: the whole workflow set moved into /.claude/ -- notes (summary/tasks/history) out of
# 0_TODO, plus 1_REVIEW and 2_ARTIFACTS wholesale. One hidden dir, so a newcomer browsing the repo
# sees code first. The catch-all still ignores 0_OVERNIGHT_WORK and anything else numbered.
[0-9]_*/
vck5000/host/benchmarks/mms/

# /.claude/1_REVIEW/ -- the REPORTS ARE TRACKED (Mark, 2026-08-07). The negation must come after
# the catch-all above AND must win on the DIRECTORY: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a re-include of a file inside one can never fire. Once git descends, everything
# under it is tracked unless re-excluded below.
!/.claude/1_REVIEW/

# ...except archive/, which is 161 MB of placement GIFs and visualizations, not reports.
/.claude/1_REVIEW/archive/

# /.claude/0_WORKFLOW/ -- summary/tasks/history/rules ARE TRACKED (2026-08-14). Same rule as
# 1_REVIEW above: re-include the directory so git descends, then re-exclude noteToSelf.md, the
# personal scratchpad Mark doesn't review.
!/.claude/0_WORKFLOW/
/.claude/0_WORKFLOW/noteToSelf.md

# /.claude/2_ARTIFACTS/ is NOT tracked -- 1.9 GB of GIFs, PNGs and DEFs, all regenerable output
# (`tools/generate_viz.py`, the viz-gif skill). Already ignored by the catch-all; stated here so
# nobody "fixes" the asymmetry with 1_REVIEW by adding a negation. Git blobs are forever: a commit
# of this would stay in the pack after any later removal, and only a history rewrite reclaims it.

# Local-only Claude Code settings, and the Obsidian vault config.
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/.obsidian/
